menu "Chime Bluetooth"
config CHIME_LDAC_APLL_FOLLOW
    bool "Experimental LDAC48k direct PCM with seamless APLL clock recovery"
    depends on IDF_TARGET_ESP32S31 && CHIME_BT_VENDOR_CODECS && !CHIME_LDAC_PIPELINE_TEST
    default y
    help
        LDAC 48k consumes PCM one-for-one, without software drift FIR. A slow
        buffer controller adjusts only APLL SDM within +/-300ppm. USB feedback
        follows the output clock model plus its FIFO servo. Requires the single
        I2S0 master/APLL owner and the unchanged DSP input ASRC configuration.
        Unsupported clock plans/rates use the fixed-clock FIR path. STOP,
        tone and source changes restore nominal SDM before releasing I2S.
        Enabled by default for board validation. Mixed-stream and fixed-clock
        DSP-output acceptance are still required; disable to restore drift FIR.

config CHIME_LDAC_PIPELINE_TEST
    bool "TEST ONLY: CPU1 LDAC48k decode+exact SRC, bounded ready48k bridge"
    depends on IDF_TARGET_ESP32S31 && CHIME_BT_VENDOR_CODECS && !FREERTOS_UNICORE
    default n
    help
        Controlled architecture experiment. One CPU1 worker services SRC between
        LDAC frames; CPU0 only consumes prepared blocks and writes mixed I2S.
        Keeps the 192-tap Q30 FIR and exact PCM mathematics. CPU1 PIE is selected
        only after startup bit-exact checks and complete-path measurement.
        LDAC 48k only; other rates/codecs retain their original path.

config CHIME_LDAC_DOT_INTERPOLATION_TEST
    bool "TEST ONLY: interpolate full Q30 FIR dot products (<=26 Q27 LSB bound)"
    depends on CHIME_LDAC_PIPELINE_TEST
    default n
    help
        Same 192 taps, Q30 coefficients and continuous phase. Moves linear
        interpolation after the two endpoint FIR sums, deferring per-tap integer
        truncation. NOT bit-exact to the scalar reference: analytical worst-case
        difference <=26 Q27 LSB (-134dBFS), far below the PCM16 decoder step.
        Actual-chip bounded-error selftest and full-kernel timing are required.

config CHIME_LDAC_REPLAY_TEST
    bool "TEST ONLY: timed LDAC replay ingress (trusted LAN)"
    depends on CHIME_BT_VENDOR_CODECS && !FREERTOS_UNICORE
    default n
    help
        Explicit HTTP start/stop and bounded ahead-of-time packet ingress.
        Feeds the real LDAC decoder from an independent ESP timer, not from
        PCM demand. Never fakes a BT connection; not RF/phone acceptance.
        No autostart. Disabled builds expose no replay control endpoints.

config CHIME_LDAC_REPLAY_FLASH
    bool "TEST ONLY: preloaded, seam-qualified LDAC fixture"
    depends on CHIME_LDAC_REPLAY_TEST
    default n
    help
        Read-only test data partition at 0x400000, 8MiB. Requires the separate
        bench partition CSV and an explicitly pinned, qualified 48k/31s file.
        No runtime HTTP supply; no automatic partition creation or flash write.
config CHIME_LDAC_REPLAY_FLASH_SHA256
    string "Qualified fixture payload SHA256"
    depends on CHIME_LDAC_REPLAY_FLASH
    default ""

config CHIME_BT_DELAY_EXTRA_MS
    int "Calibrated receiver delay correction (ms)"
    range 0 500
    default 0
    help
        Added to observed application residence/PCM queue delay and nominal
        4x128-frame I2S DMA (10.667ms). Default 0 is UNCALIBRATED, not zero
        actual codec/protocol-stack/DSP latency. Set only after AV measurement.
        Reports do not include phone encoder/transmit latency. Internal SBC
        cannot observe raw packet residence and has less complete estimates.

config CHIME_BT_VENDOR_CODECS
    bool "Experimental aptX / aptX HD / Android Opus / LDAC sink"
    depends on BT_A2DP_USE_EXTERNAL_CODEC
    default y
    help
        Project-local hash-pinned stack replacements; six SEPs (seven with LHDC V5). All seven backends use the pinned ESP32-S31-A2DP-Codecs import.
          Vendor formats remain 44.1/48k stereo PCM16. No aptX LL.
        libfreeaptx is LGPL-2.1-or-later. Review redistribution requirements.
        Disable for the unpatched SBC/AAC recovery build.
config CHIME_BT_LHDC_V5
    bool "Experimental S31 LHDC V5 decoder (not V2/V3)"
    depends on CHIME_BT_VENDOR_CODECS
    default y
    help
        Adds a seventh sink SEP. 44.1/48k stereo PCM16, 256..500 kbps,
        V5 version 1, 5ms. No lossless, metadata, AR or low-latency mode.
        Pinned S31 source; known PCM16 level regression against existing
          independent encoder fixtures (see migration document).
        NOT a licensed/certified LHDC product; hardware validation required.
        Disable this option for a six-codec build without LHDC.
endmenu

menu "Chime physical controls"
config CHIME_ENCODER_REVERSE
    bool "Reverse side encoder direction"
    default n
    help
        Provisional A/B direction. Enable if user-relative forward rolling
        decreases volume on the assembled speaker. No hardware rewiring needed.
endmenu
